description:
Compare 16-bit sequence numbers across the wrap and filter out duplicates and stale packets (lesson 5.02).

```cpp
int sequenceDifference(std::uint16_t a, std::uint16_t b);
bool sequenceGreater(std::uint16_t a, std::uint16_t b);

class DuplicateFilter
{
public:
    bool accept(std::uint16_t sequence);
    std::optional<std::uint16_t> latest() const;
};
```

- **sequenceDifference** is `a - b` computed in 16 bits and read as a signed 16-bit number: from -32768 to 32767.
- **sequenceGreater** is true when `a` is newer than `b`: their difference is positive. (Exactly half way round counts as greater in neither direction.)
- **DuplicateFilter** remembers the latest sequence number accepted and which of the 256 numbers ending at it (latest - 255 to latest) have been seen. `accept` returns true and records the number if it has not been seen: the first number ever, a newer one (which becomes the latest), or an older one inside the window that is not yet marked. It returns false for a number already seen or one 256 or more behind the latest. `latest` is empty until something is accepted.

